  "description": "Audit a UI already built and rendered, not one being designed. Use when asked to check, verify, review, or QA an existing page/screen \u2014 \"does this look right,\" \"review this screenshot,\" \"check the deployed page,\" \"compare against the design,\" \"why did this break on refresh\" \u2014 or when handed a screenshot/image/live URL for visual review, even without the words \"audit\" or \"QA\" (\"does the build look OK,\" \"spot check this page\"). Treats a build succeeding or the DOM having the right elements as weak evidence \u2014 only actually looking at the rendered result counts as proof. Covers: toasts vanishing before a screenshot lands; measuring the gap against a reference design instead of \"looks worse\"; SPA view-switches that never update the URL, breaking refresh/deep-link/back; broken vs. not-yet-triggered lazy images; and staying honest about what a still image can't prove. Audit-only by default \u2014 no editing, installing, or fixing unless explicitly asked.",
